From 0d3735426835aff0bd8151a0203e0720b157315f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Allen Winter <winter@kde.org>
Date: Tue, 24 Feb 2026 10:22:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Start adding fuzzer testing for the vcard library (#1225)

* Start adding fuzzer testing for the vcard library

* vcardstructured.c: return from new_from_string early for empty string

* vcardstructuredimpl.h: use dynamically sized array for fields

The vcardstructured_impl struct used a fixed-size array to store
fields but it did not impose a limit on the maximum number of fields.
Now, it dynamically manages the field array and reallocates the
buffer if required.

* vcardparser.c: reject BEGIN/END content lines with no TEXT value

* initialize the errbuf so we don't write a null pointer

If there's a parsing error, _parse_error calls

    buf_vprintf(&state->errbuf, fmt, ap);

which attempts vsnprintf(buf->s... and buf->s is 0x0.

This fixes:

    The following tests FAILED:
        108 - vcfuzz1test480258833 (SEGFAULT)
        111 - vcfuzz1test485932113 (SEGFAULT)

when compiled with:

  cmake -B build --warn-uninitialized -Werror=dev -G Ninja -DLIBICAL_DEVMODE_MEMORY_CONSISTENCY=True -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug -DLIBICAL_DEVMODE=True -DLIBICAL_ENABLE_BUILTIN_TZDATA=True  -DLIBICAL_GLIB_BUILD_DOCS=False -DLIBICAL_GLIB=False -DLIBICAL_GOBJECT_INTROSPECTION=False -DLIBICAL_GLIB_VAPI=False -DLIBICAL_BUILD_TESTING_BIGFUZZ=True

* vcardcomponent_fuzz1.c: free memory at end of test to avoid ASAN error

* vcardparser.c: reset 'version' property in case of error

* [pre-commit.ci] auto fixes from pre-commit.com hooks

for more information, see https://pre-commit.ci

* src/test/libicalvcard/CMakeLists.txt - temporarily remove 485932113

we'll work 485932113 in a separate patch

